// Package llmclient ports core/llm_client.py — provider clients,
// detection, timeouts, extract_json (T-30, Phase 3).
//
// Spec: docs/port-blueprint/module-specs/spec-core-llm-client.md.
//
// THE PACKAGE LAWS:
//   - The WIRE is the contract: the OpenAI/Anthropic request bodies are
//     built as ordered dicts and serialized in Python json.dumps compact
//     form (", " / ": " separators) — the payload goldens
//     (testdata/llmclient_payloads.golden.json, generated by
//     testdiff/goldens/dump_llmclient.py from the unmodified reference)
//     pin the bytes. The fake-server replies in the Go tests speak the
//     same separator law (PyDumpsCompact).
//   - The wall-clock timeout rides context deadlines (the spec's Go
//     note replacing the ThreadPoolExecutor trick); a timeout surfaces
//     as *TimeoutError with the reference's exact message. Python's
//     socket-timeout-5s-above-wall-clock dance is subsumed (timeoutS
//     <= 0 keeps the reference's 120 s socket cap as client.Timeout).
//   - Loopback never rides a proxy (the v0.15.1 law): the OpenAI paths
//     and the probes route loopback targets through a proxy-less
//     transport. The Anthropic paths keep the reference's quirk of
//     ALWAYS riding the default (env-proxy) transport — see the
//     divergence note below for the Go net/http corner.
//   - The JSON-mode memo is process-lifetime, keyed by the normalized
//     base URL; the 400 → one-clean-retry → memoize law is ported
//     exactly (ResetJSONModeMemo exists for tests).
//   - Every user-visible error string is byte-exact where the runtime
//     allows: the URLError suffix keeps the "<urlopen error …>" SHAPE
//     with Go's own inner text (runtime-shaped, unpinned); the
//     detect_ollama failure details carry the Python exception-class
//     prefixes (URLError / HTTPError / JSONDecodeError / ValueError).
//
// DOCUMENTED DIVERGENCES (Python-runtime artifacts the typed port
// collapses — each recorded here per the port law):
//   - The ollama-py SDK client object is Python-only; the port
//     implements the /api/chat + /api/tags wire directly (OllamaClient,
//     the OllamaAPI seam). The SDK's old-dict/new-object response
//     duality is ONE wire shape; ResponseContent handles it, and the
//     list extraction uses the name-or-model rule (the rule the
//     reference's own raw-HTTP detect_ollama speaks).
//   - ollama_chat's json_mode defaults ON in Python; the Go options
//     struct carries JSONModeOff (zero value = JSON on) so callers get
//     the default for free. The cloud ChatOptions keep a JSONMode bool
//     (Python's default there is OFF).
//   - ChatOptions.Temperature 0 means the 0.7 default (no caller sends
//     a literal 0.0; Python's default is 0.7 and run_golden's 0.2 rides
//     the field).
//   - The over-budget warnings, the autodetect decision messages (emoji
//     included), the probe detail lines and the limits line are
//     byte-pinned by the pure/behavior goldens.
//   - int('5_0') underscore parsing and the str.isdigit() unicode-digit
//     crash corner (a crafted tasklist PID) are not replicated; pyInt
//     handles bool/int/float/decimal-string like Python's guarded int().
//   - Go's ProxyFromEnvironment never proxies loopback addresses by
//     net/http law, so an anthropic-shaped LOOPBACK URL with a proxy
//     env var behaves DIRECT here where the reference would attempt the
//     proxy — unreachable in the app's own flows (cloud URLs are never
//     loopback); recorded for honesty.
//   - The Windows tasklist/netstat and POSIX ss/netstat subprocess
//     parsing is kept for parity (the spec's Go note), with
//     CREATE_NO_WINDOW on Windows (build-tagged noWindowAttr).
package llmclient
